====================================================================================================
   tau = 3.5417 us, w0 = 1.7708 mJ/m^3, J.E(0) = 1000.0 W/m^3, 2w0/tau = 1000.0
PASS  tau = eps/sigma = 3.54 us
PASS  w(0) = 1/2 eps E0^2 = 1.77 mJ/m^3
PASS  J.E(0) = sigma E0^2 = 1000 W/m^3 = 2 w0/tau
PASS  energy halves every (tau/2) ln 2 = 1.23 us; charge every tau ln 2 = 2.45 us
PASS  conduction sigma E and displacement eps dE/dt cancel at every t (so H = 0, S = 0)
PASS  dw/dt = -J.E at every t (theorem with S = 0)
PASS  all of w(0) ends up as heat: int sigma E^2 dt = w(0)

