K. Section 6: the notes' Example 1, J_s = x 2 cos(wt) A/m on z = 0 in vacuum
====================================================================================================
PASS  (a) E = -x eta0 cos(wt -+ beta z), H = -+ y cos(wt -+ beta z) (Lecture 19 recipe, np.cross)
PASS  (b) S = E x H = +- z eta0 cos^2(wt -+ beta z), never toward the sheet
