Q. Example: two equal waves in opposite directions (standing wave)
====================================================================================================
PASS  E = x 2E0 sin wt sin bz, H = y (2E0/eta) cos wt cos bz, S = z (E0^2/eta) sin 2wt sin 2bz = (|E1|^2 - |E2|^2)/eta
PASS  the standing-wave fields satisfy the source-free Maxwell equations
PASS  <S> = 0 and <w> = eps E0^2 at every z
PASS  S changes sign every quarter period
PASS  where sin bz = 0, w = 0 at the instants cos wt = 0
PASS  energy in any half wavelength is constant in time (= eps E0^2 lambda/2)

